अक्खल्ल्कृत्या
<p>अक्खल्ल्कृत्या /akkhallkṛtyā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>akkhalıkřtyā, s. u. akhkhalão Nachtr.</p>

अक्तुः
<p>अक्तुः /aktuḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aktúhl: Ererbter -u-Stamm im Ai. und Lat. (noctū) ist zweifel<br>haft, s. Wack. II/2, 667, Szemerényi, Glo. 38 (1960) 113 Anm. 3; zu beachten Minard, BSL 51 (1955), c.-r. 36.</p>

अक्राः
<p>अक्राः /akrāḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>akráh: s. Bailey, BSOAS 24 (1961) 472 Anm. 9; P. Friedrich,<br>Proto-Indo-European Trees (1970) 66f.</p>

अक्षम्
<p>अक्षम् /akṣam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>akṣam: s. auch Duchesne-Guillemin, Hommages à G. Dumézil<br>(1960) 96f., Belardi, AION 3 (1961) 2, sowie die Lit. bei Turner, IAL 2a.</p>

अक्षि
<p>अक्षि /akṣi/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-12.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-12.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ákṣi: vgl. Gunnarsson, NTS 24 (1971) 66f., mit Lit.</p>

अक्षुः
<p>अक्षुः /akṣuḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-13.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-13.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áksuh: s. Wüst, Pñua 2 (1956) 67 Anm. 19; Sharma, Põua 5/6<br>(1959/60) 272.</p>

अख्खलीकृत्या
<p>अख्खलीकृत्या /akhkhalīkṛtyā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-14.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-14.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>akhkhalīkřtyā (akkhalio? Hiersche, Aspirata 88[f.] u. Anm. 30,<br>mit Lit.): dazu Mehendale, Belvalkar-Vol. 12 ff. (s. Hiersche a.a. 0. Anm. 31), sowie (unglaubhaft) Wright, NCSL 12.</p>

अगरी, गरा, गरी
<p>अगरी, गरा, गरी /agarī/ /garā/ /garī/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-15.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-15.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>agarī, garā, garī [s.o. I 324, s. v. garalam] Andropogon<br>serratus (Lex.), s. DED-Suppl. 51 a (zur dravid. Sippe von mal. karuka ,Agrostis linearis' usw.?).</p>

अगस्तिः
<p>अगस्तिः /agastiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-16.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-16.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>agástih: zu ved. Agástya- m. Name eines Rși (vom Baum<br>namen (vgl. auch Turner, IAL 3a]?) s. überkühne Kombinationen bei Wright, BSOAS 30 (1967) 543.</p>

अगारम्
<p>अगारम् /agāram/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-17.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-623-17.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>agāram: vgl. L. Lombardo, RIL 91 (1957) 234f.</p>

अगुरुः
<p>अगुरुः /aguruḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aguruh: zur dravid. Deutung auch Burrow, Skr. 380 fund<br>3. Aufl. (1973) 381]; zur Ausbreitung des Kulturwortes Filliozat, JA 246 (1958) 85ff., vgl. noch Schwarzschild, IIJ 8 (1964) 27 u. Anm. 11. — Anders L. Lombardo, RIL 91 (1957) 235.</p>

अग्निः
<p>अग्निः /agniḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>agnih: zur Grundform s. noch Loicq, L'antiquité classique 31<br>(1962) 131 u. Anm. 3, 4; Hamp, Baltic Linguistics (ed. T. F. Magner u. W. R. Schmalstieg, 1970) 75ff. – Die Zugehörigkeit von Aloniš in heth. Texten ist umstritten; s. die Lit. in MIAV 129 a, 144 a, Kammenhuber, Arier 150 ff., Mayrhofer, Mythos 14 Anm. 14.</p>

अग्रिमः
<p>अग्रिमः /agrimaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>agrimáḥ: s. Kuiper, IIJ 7 (1963/64) 320.</p>

अग्र्यः
<p>अग्र्यः /agryaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>agryáh: indo-iran. Parallelen bei Jamasp Asa-Humbach, Pur<br>sišnihā I (1971) 49 Anm.</p>

अघः
<p>अघः /aghaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>agháḥ, s. u. zu ághrā. -- Vgl. Burrow, TPS 1949, 59.</p>

अघ्न्यः
<p>अघ्न्यः /aghnyaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ághnyaḥ: monographisch H.-P. Schmidt, KZ 78 (1963) 1ff.,<br>45; zuletzt Narten, Acta Orientalia Neerlandica (1971) 120 ff., mit reicher Lit.</p>

अघ्रा, अघ्रा
<p>अघ्रा, अघ्रा /aghrā/ /aghrā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ághrā (aghrá ?) f. Not, Übel, Drangsal (TA; Sharma,<br>Pñua 5/6 (1959/60] 4f.), = aw. ayrā- f. Name einer Krankheit, vgl. got, agló f. ,Drangsal', zu agháḥ; Sharma a.a. 0. 5, mit Lit.</p>

अङ्कः
<p>अङ्कः /aṅkaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ankah m. Scheinkampf im Drama, mimischer Kampf<br>(Lex.); zu den dravid. Wörtern für Schlacht, Kampf' (tamil ankam usw.), nach DED 4b (Nr. 31)?</p>

अङ्गारकः
<p>अङ्गारकः /aṅgārakaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>angārakaḥ, s. bhrngarājaḥ, o. II 518.</p>

अङ्गारः
<p>अङ्गारः /aṅgāraḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ángārah, s. Eilers, Gs. Güntert 307 Anm. 1 (,,als irani<br>sches Lehnwort ansprechbar").</p>

अङ्गिराः
<p>अङ्गिराः /aṅgirāḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ángirāḥ: s. H.-P. Schmidt, Bphaspati und Indra (1968) 51f.</p>

अङ्गुलिः
<p>अङ्गुलिः /aṅguliḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-12.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-12.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>angulin, angusthá- : *angid - im Neuind. (Turner, IAL 7b;<br>*anguz-di. ~ angus-thá- {doch s. Hiersche, Aspirata 134]?).</p>

अङ्गूषः
<p>अङ्गूषः /aṅgūṣaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-13.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-13.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>angūs aḥ ( anko, o. I 545): vgl. auch nakuláh (II 122), maggusah (II 545), s. Berger, WZKSOA 3 (1959) 68 u. Anm. 131.</p>

अङ्गोषी
<p>अङ्गोषी /aṅgoṣī/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-14.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-14.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>angoși, s. o. I 554 zu ängūṣáh und Bailey, BSOAS 20 (1957) 52f.</p>

अङ्घ्रिः
<p>अङ्घ्रिः /aṅghriḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-15.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-624-15.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>anghriḥ: s. Szemerényi, Syncope 240 Anm. 1; Rix, MSS 27<br>(1970) 96.</p>

अच्छरा, अच्छला
<p>अच्छरा, अच्छला /accharā/ /acchalā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>accharā, acchálā, s. u. die Nachtr. zu rkșálā.</p>

अच्छः
<p>अच्छः /acchaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>acchaḥ2: s. Tedesco, JAOS 77 (1957) 197f.; Turner, IAL 8a;<br>Hiersche, Aspirata 113.</p>

अच्छा
<p>अच्छा /acchā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ácchå: Hiersche, Aspirata 107f.</p>

अजमोदः
<p>अजमोदः /ajamodaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ajamodaḥ m., dā f. Ligusticum ajowan (u.a.] (Suśr.,<br>u.a.), Lex. oikā f. dss., pāli ajamoja-m.,cummin-seed', usw.: s. Turner, IAL 8b, dessen Verweise auf ein volksetymologisch eingeordnetes Fremdwort schließen lassen (~ ajājih?).</p>

अजः
<p>अजः /ajaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ajáh, wohl = aw, aza- in einem Fragment, K. Hoffmann, MSS<br>22 (1967) 30, 33; s. u. die Nachtr. zu ajinam. — Zur idg. Form s. Schmitt-Brandt 106. — Gegen ajá- ,unborn (Horsch, IIJ 9 [1965] 6, 14) s. Kuiper, IIJ 9, 30f.; vgl. auch Schmitt 181f. Anm. 1075.</p>

अजाजिः, अजाजी
<p>अजाजिः, अजाजी /ajājiḥ/ /ajājī/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ajājih, ": vgl. Turner, IAL 8b; s.o. ajamodah.</p>

अजिनम्
<p>अजिनम् /ajinam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ajinam: dazu aw. azina-vant- = Fellträger', K. Hoffmann,<br>MSS 22 (1967) 31. Urspr. ,,*Ziegenfell" (: ajáho), woraus schon in indoiran. Zeit allgemein Fell', Hoffmann a.a. 0. 32.</p>

अञ्चति
<p>अञ्चति /añcati/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áñcati: zu biegen auch die Sonderbedeutung ,(Wasser) schöpfen', K. Hoffmann, KZ 79 (1965) 171 ff. (zum Etymon<br>74). - Pisani, Fs. Kuiper 102 nimmt primäres, von añoverschiedenes ac- „schöpfen' an (doch s. ved. ud-añcana- m. ,Schöpfkelleu.a., Hoffmann a.a.O. 171 Anm. 2), das zu heth. eku- ,trinken' gehöre(?).</p>

अञ्जलिः
<p>अञ्जलिः /añjaliḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>a njaliņ: vgl. die Deutung bei Rhys Davids-Stede, The Pali<br>Text Society's Pali-English Dictionary (1925) 13a (*rñjo, „zum Gebet, zur Verehrung ausgestreckt sein" (s. auch W.P. Schmid, Untersuchungen zur Stellung der Nasalpraesentien im indo-iran. Verbalsystem, Diss. Tübingen 1955, 125]); vgl. im folgenden die Nachtr. zu áñjah.</p>

अञ्जः, अञ्जषा
<p>अञ्जः, अञ्जषा /añjaḥ/ /añjaṣā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>á ñ jaḥ, áñjasā: Geldners Deutung aus *rñjaso (o. I 545) stützt<br>Insler, KZ 82 (1968) 1 ff. (áĩjasã:rõasẫmáu = mảmasã: namasāná. u.a.; áñjo in identischen Kontexten mit rjüyá, rájistha-). - S. o. die Nachtr. zu añjalih; vgl. sam-añjasa-, 0. III 435 (s.v. sám).</p>

अट्टम्
<p>अट्टम् /aṭṭam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>attam: s. Wüst, Põua 3 (1957) 50 Anm. 4, Kuiper, IIJ 7<br>(1963/64) 324; wichtig v. a. Scheller, KZ 79 (1965) 224 ff., bes. 236 ff.</p>

अट्टः
<p>अट्टः /aṭṭaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-12.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-625-12.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>attaḥ(1) („[Wacht]Turm"): s. Skelton, AION 6 (1965) 23 ff. -<br>Hierher (?) auch attapāla- (Schmidt 13a), „etwa Marktaufseher“ S. Scheller, KZ 80 (1966) 257ff.</p>

अट्टः
<p>अट्टः /aṭṭaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>attah(2) trocken (Lex.), prākr. attaï wird trocken, u.a.;<br>dravid., vgl. tamil atu ,to cook' etc. (DED 7b Nr. 66)?</p>

अड्डनम्
<p>अड्डनम् /aḍḍanam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>addanam: s. Turner, IAL 10b.</p>

अण्डम्, आण्डम्
<p>अण्डम्, आण्डम् /aṇḍam/ /āṇḍam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>andám, ved. ão: vgl. Turner, IAL 50 af., mit Lit.; Burrow,<br>BSOAS 34 (1971) 545 (: Aitareya-Ar. ānda- ,egg').</p>

अण्डीरः, आण्डीरः
<p>अण्डीरः, आण्डीरः /aṇḍīraḥ/ /āṇḍīraḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>andīraḥ (ão) unkastriert, männlich (Lex.), als , testicu<br>latus' zu andam (Wack. II/2, 461, Mayrhofer, Kratylos 6 [1961] 158); die ursprünglich (DED 11b) als Quelle von ao vermutete dravid. Sippe (kui andra ,male animal' usw.) stammt aus dem Indoarischen (Burrow-Emeneau, JAOS 92 [1972] 477b).</p>

अतति
<p>अतति /atati/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>átati: zu beachten Wüst, Pñua 4 (1958) 100 Anm. 46; s. Hum.<br>bach, MSS 9 (1956) 74 Anm. 10, Gathas II 8 (: aw.hu-ab-ra-).</p>

अतसम्
<p>अतसम् /atasam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>atasám: s. Wüst, Pñua 4 (1958) 71.</p>

अतिथिः
<p>अतिथिः /atithiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>átithiḥ: s. Wüst, Põua 4 (1958) 71, Wack. II/2, 722; hierher<br>auch ved. Atithigvá- N. pr. (Wack. II/2, 545). – Zur Diskussion von átithi. und seinen Entsprechungen in Eigennamen s. MLAV 130 a, Kammenhuber, Arier 168ff., 254a.</p>

अत्कः
<p>अत्कः /atkaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>átkaḥ: Monographisch Wüst, Põua 4 (1958) 59ff., mit reichster<br>Lit. (der anzufügen ist: Čop, Ling. 1 [1955] 28, 3 [1958] 66 zu átka-2 ,Axt, schneidige Waffe', nach Pischel, Ved. Stud. II 193ff.; dagegen Wüst a.a.O. 63f.]; van Windekens, AION 1 (1959] 17; Gershevitch, Fs. Pagliaro II (1969] 201, dagegen OnP 179).</p>

अत्यः
<p>अत्यः /atyaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>átyaḥ: s. auch vyátiḥ, o. III 272. – Vgl. Wüst, Piua 4<br>(1958) 72.</p>

अत्रिः
<p>अत्रिः /atriḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>Átriḥ m. Name eines Rși (RV, usw.; nirgends sicher ,verzehrend' [o. I 28], s. Wack. II/2, 710); vgl. Wüst, Pñua 4 (1958) 50.</p>

अत्सरा
<p>अत्सरा /atsarā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>atsárā, s. u. die Nachtr. zu rksálā.</p>

अथर्वा
<p>अथर्वा /atharvā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-12.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-626-12.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>átharva: Erwägungen eines *athar- ,Feuer' bei Sharma,<br>Põua 5/6 (1959/60) 14 (Ś. S. athar-vy-usta- ,,vom Feuer verbrannt?), Renou, ÉVédP. 13 (1964) 52, 137 (athar-yú- ,fait de flammes), Minard, BSL 61 (1966) c.-. 18; anders Bailey, TPS 1956, 89f. (*athar- ,power of apotrope). Vgl. auch Benveniste, instit. I 282 (< Iran.?). — S. noch Gershevitch, Fs. Pagliaro II (1969) 189f. (der aus elam. Namen ein iran. *aparva[n] = ved. átharo gewinnt; dazu OnP 122, 132, 158); Wack. I? Nachtr. ad 120, 6-8, pg. 66.</p>

अदः
<p>अदः /adaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>adáh: s. Wack. I? Nachtr. ad 340, 39—41, pg. 193.</p>

अदितिः
<p>अदितिः /aditiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áditiḥ: s.o. II 39f. und Minard, BSL 61 (1966) c.-r. 18.</p>

अद्धा
<p>अद्धा /addhā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>addhá: s. Bailey, Fs. Taqizadeh (1962) 35; Szemerényi,<br>Sprache 12 (1966) 203 ff., mit Lit. - Über addhā kar(Ganapātha) ~ ap. azdā kar-, iran. *azda-kära- Bekannt. macher, Bote' s. K. Hoffmann, MSS 12 (1956) 53, bzw. W.P. Schmid bei Happ, Glo. 40 (1962) 200, Szemerényi a.a.O. 204 u. Anm. 76.</p>

अद्भुतः
<p>अद्भुतः /adbhutaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ádbhutaḥ: zu den indo-iran. Textfiguren (o. I 547) s. noch<br>Schlerath II 155 b. Vgl. auch Strunk 66. — Hierher aw. abda,miraculous' < *a-dbda. (: -dbhuta-) nach Bailey bei Gershevitch, Fs. Pagliaro II (1969) 181(?).</p>

अद्मसद्-
<p>अद्मसद्- /admasad-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>admasád- f. Fliege (RV), < ,,*die sich ans Essen<br>(ádma) setzt“ (osád-, o. III 473): Thieme, KZ 79 (1965) 220 ff., mit Lit.; unterstützt durch neuind. Fortsetzer wie nepāli aữso ,maggot, insect, worm' (Turner, IAL 12b, dazu Kuiper, IIJ 7 [1963/64] 320, Mayrhofer, Kratylos 12 [1967] 55f. Anm. 1).</p>

अद्युः
<p>अद्युः /adyuḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ádyuh (o. I 548), s. Kellens, Diss. 585f.</p>

अधस्तात्
<p>अधस्तात् /adhastāt/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>adhástāt: Verweis richtiger auf hesta (o. III 611).</p>

अध्रिः, अध्रिज्-, अध्रिगु-
<p>अध्रिः, अध्रिज्-, अध्रिगु- /adhriḥ/ /adhrij-/ /adhrigu-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ádhriḥ, adhrij., ádhrigu-: s. Wüst, Pñua 3 (1957) 117ff.;<br>4 (1958) 5ff., 40 ff., 50 ff., mit reicher Lit. [Dazu Bailey, Studies in Indo-Asian Art and Culture 2 (Acharya RaghuVira Comm. Vol., New Delhi 1973) 15ff.].</p>

अध्वरः
<p>अध्वरः /adhvaraḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>adhvaráh: s. die Lit. bei Minard, BSL 51 (1955) c.-r. 37.</p>

अध्वा
<p>अध्वा /adhvā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ádhvā: s. Rix, MSS 27 (1970) 100.</p>

अन-
<p>अन- /ana-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ana-: ein ererbter Pronominalstamm ana- ist anzweifelbar, s.<br>Wack. III 526 ff. und die Lit. in ApH. 102f.</p>

अनलः
<p>अनलः /analaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-12.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-12.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>analah: gegen die Deutung als „unersättlich" Edgerton,<br>JAOS 79 (1959) 41 aff.; s. auch Kuiper, Kratylos 4 (1959) 167.</p>

अनवपृग्नः
<p>अनवपृग्नः /anavapṛgnaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-13.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-13.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ánavaprgnaḥ, s. prņákti, o. II 330.</p>

अनिलः
<p>अनिलः /anilaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-14.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-14.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ánilah: nach Chantraine I 86 b viell. dissimiliert aus *ánima<br>(= gr. ávejos)[?]. - [S. jetzt Insler, Sprache 20 (1974) 115ff.].</p>

अनूपः
<p>अनूपः /anūpaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-15.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-15.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>anūpáḥ: s. Frei, Studii ṣi cercetari lingvistice 11, 3(= Omagiu<br>lui Al. Graur, 1960)475ff., Cahiers F. de Saussure 17(1960)47ff.; dazu Buddruss, KZ 77 (1961) 236, 245, GS Ind. 1 (1973) 33.</p>

अन्तरिक्षम्
<p>अन्तरिक्षम् /antarikṣam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-16.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-627-16.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>antárikṣam: s. Minard, BSL 51 (1955) c.-r. 37, 55 (1960) c.-r.<br>65. Vgl. die Lit. bei Kuiper, Noun-inflexion 91 Anm. 1.</p>

अन्ती
<p>अन्ती /antī/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>anti: s. Bonveniste, Hitt. 107.</p>

अन्त्रम्
<p>अन्त्रम् /antram/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>antrám (ep., kl.; RV usw. antrá-, Wackernagel, KZ 59, 23<br>Anm. 1 = KI. Schr. 343 Anm. 1, Ai. Gramm. II/2, 710): 8. auch u. die Nachtr. zu yakýt.</p>

अन्दोलयति
<p>अन्दोलयति /andolayati/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>andolayati usw. (o. I 549]: s. Berger, ZDMG 112 (1962)<br>419 f. [o. III 597]; Słuszkiewicz, Prace filologiczne 18,4 (1965) 135 ff.</p>

अन्धः
<p>अन्धः /andhaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ándhaḥ: wegen der ved. Bedeutung (,,the juice of the soma<br>plant", Burrow, ArchLing. 6 (1954] 61) wird die Gleichsetzung mit gr. avtos angezweifelt; s. Aitchison, Glo. 41 (1963) 276ff., Szemerényi, Syncope 7 Anm. 2.</p>

अन्धः
<p>अन्धः /andhaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>andháḥ (und RV ándhas- n. ,Dunkel): Iranisches (wie khotan<br>sak. hana., sogd. 'nt ,blind' u.a.) bei Eilers, BZN 15 (1964) 201 Anm. 67, Bailey, Zamb. 384. — Zu gall. andabata s. Guyonvarc'h, Ogam 15 (1963) 107ff.; vgl. noch Wüst, Pñua 4 (1958) 101 Anm. 54, van Windekens, Orbis 11 (1962) 522f. - Hierher als „Blindfluß" die Flußnamen Andhanadi. f. und viell. *Andhamati- in Arrians 'Avdouaris, Eilers a. a. 0. 219.</p>

अन्नम्
<p>अन्नम् /annam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ánnam: *anda- im Neuind. ist als Beweis des Etymons *adna<br>(anders Wüst, Põua 4 [1958] 100 Anm. 44) anzweifelbar, s. Mayrhofer, Kratylos 12 (1967) 56 Anm. 2 (zu Turner, IAL 18b).</p>

अन्यत्र
<p>अन्यत्र /anyatra/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>anyátra = buddh. sogd. 'nys elsewhere', Gershevitch 47.</p>

अन्यह्
<p>अन्यह् /anyah/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>anyáḥ: sogd. 'nyw anderer (Gershevitch 11), khotansak. aña-;<br>vgl. noch ved. anyá-jāta. = āštiyāni anazā, Morgenstierne, Fs. Taqizadeh 208 Anm. 3. – Zu ved. anyá-law. anya- in Textfiguren s.o. I 532, Schlerath II 158 b.</p>

अपवान्
<p>अपवान् /apavān/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ápavān: zu aw. afant- s. noch Pisani, ZDMG 107 (1957) 551f.<br>(mit Lit.), Gershevitch, Hymn 172f., 174, 322f., Benveniste, Oss. 75f. Anm. 5, Szemerényi, KZ 76 (1960) 61 ff.</p>

अपाष्ठः
<p>अपाष्ठः /apāṣṭhaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>apăṣtháḥ: s. Hiersche, Aspirata 57f., 134f.</p>

अपि
<p>अपि /api/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ápil, s. Gonda, Lingua 21 (1968) 183ff.</p>

अपिकक्षः
<p>अपिकक्षः /apikakṣaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-12.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-12.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>apikakṣáḥ, s. u. kákṣā Nachtr.</p>

अपूपः
<p>अपूपः /apūpaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-13.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-628-13.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>apūpáh: nach Kölver, MSS 30 (1972) 111 ff., 114, 115ff., 122f.<br>ist apūpá. ~ pūpa. mi. Entwicklung aus apivāpa- (TB) ~ *pivāpa-, zu vap- ,hinstreuen' (also ,,*Hingestreutes" ,,dünner, flacher Kuchen“); a.a.O. 115 und 126 Anm. 12 (mit Lit.) gegen dravid. Deutung.</p>

अप्नः
<p>अप्नः /apnaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ápnaḥ: zur Verbindung mit heth. happinant. und gr. & qevos<br>8. die Lit. bei Frisk III 45 und Chantraine I 146b; dazu Manessy-Guitton, ILJ 8 (1964/65) 184 ff., IF 71 (1966) 22 ff.</p>

अप्वा
<p>अप्वा /apvā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>apvá: unter Anerkennung von K. Hoffmanns Bedeutungs<br>bestimmung für ao und ap. afuva- (o. I 550) schließt Bailey, BSOAS 21 (1958) 536, 23 (1960) 14ff. khotansak. ah(v)a,innermost part of the body' an, dessen Konnex wegen seiner auffallenden Bedeutung ... erst noch näher zu begründen wäre ..." (Wüst, Põua 8-11 [1966] 15 Anm. 4; s. auch Szemerényi, Syncope 309 A. 2). Vgl. Wüst a.a. 0. 13ff., mit Lit., K. Hoffmann, Mél. Renou 368 ff.</p>

अप्सराः
<p>अप्सराः /apsarāḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>Pag 07 (1962. Hars Bulletin<br>apsaráh: s. die Lit. bei Wack. II/12 Nachtr. ad 301, 32-34,<br>pg. 83; Bailey, BSOAS 21 (1958) 544f.; Manessy-Guitton, IIJ 7 (1963/64) 277; Wright, BSOAS 30 (1967) 534. - Non vidi: R. G. Harshe, A new interpretation of the word apsaras-, Adyar Library Bulletin 21 (1957) 263ff. - Zu beachten o. II 388 (zu psáras-); . u. Nachtr. zu āścaryaḥ, III 641.</p>

अप्सः
<p>अप्सः /apsaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ápsah: s. Bailey, Fs. Pagliaro I (1969) 137ff., 141 ff., 143ff.<br>(auch zu ápsas.,injury'); s.o. III 511 (zu stánah).</p>

अप्सुः
<p>अप्सुः /apsuḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ápsuh, nur in RV 7, 4, 6 (avírā ...) ápravah: nach Burrow,<br>JRAS 1969, 115f. doch ,without cattle (*-pṣu- *-psu- : paśúh).</p>

अभि
<p>अभि /abhi/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>abhi („um“): mit gr. dugi als *a,mbhí identisch, s. Rix, MSS 27<br>(1970) 90. - RV asmád abhi naw. ahmat ... a'bi, Schlerath II 155 a.</p>

अभिव्लङ्गः
<p>अभिव्लङ्गः /abhivlaṅgaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>abhivlangáh, s. noch o. III 244 (s.v. vrnákti).</p>

अभिष्टिः
<p>अभिष्टिः /abhiṣṭiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>abhiṣṭih, s. Hiersche, Aspirata 64.</p>

अभीक्ष्णम्
<p>अभीक्ष्णम् /abhīkṣṇam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>abhiksnam: s. Wack. I? Nachtr. ad 43, 43 und 60, 10, pg. 26,<br>37; Minard, BSL 51 (1955) c.-r. 37.</p>

अभ्रम्
<p>अभ्रम् /abhram/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>abhrám, s. u. zu ámbhah, III 630.</p>

अभ्रिः
<p>अभ्रिः /abhriḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ábhrih: vgl. Wüst, Pñua 4 (1958) 31.</p>

अभ्वः
<p>अभ्वः /abhvaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-12.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-12.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ábhvah:s. Wüst, Pñua 4 (1958) 100 Anm. 47; Kuiper, Lingua<br>11 (1962) 229, 230 (auch zu AV abhvd-).</p>

अमतिः
<p>अमतिः /amatiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-13.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-13.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>amátiḥ (,,Schein"?) bleibt nach wie vor unklar (Wack. II/2<br>641), da vy-āmá ,Abschwörung und sam-āmá-, Vertragseid, auf amt. „sich eidlich binden' zu beziehen sind (o. III 438). - Vgl. noch Minard, BSL 51 (1955) c.-r, 38, Venkatasubbiah, Adyar Library Bulletin 26 (1962) 211 ff. = Vedic Studies II (Madras 1968) 1 ff. [s. Kuiper, IIJ 14 (1972) 89, mit Lit.], G. Ito, Acta Asiatica (Tokyo) 26 (1974) 57 ff.</p>

अमः
<p>अमः /amaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-14.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-629-14.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ámahi (,,Angriffskraft“, K. Hoffmann, KZ 83 [1969] 196),<br>s. Schlerath II 162b.</p>

अमः
<p>अमः /amaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ámah: dazu ap. ama-ta ,von da an', Kent 169, ApH. 102.</p>

अमीति
<p>अमीति /amīti/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ámiti: dazu monographisch K. Hoffmann, KZ 83 (1969) 193ff.<br>(193f. zum Formenbestand; RV abhi ami. = ,anpacken, angreifen [195], Samh. pari ami. = ,ringsum anpacken“; dazu das Kaus. ved. āmáyati ,tut weh' [197]. Die restlichen Belege bedeuten „schwören' [v. a. sám ami. „sich eidlich binden, zusammen schwören“, 197ff.] und sind mit gr. ouvõue, ouó-oau [*agema;-) zu verbinden [209, mit reicher Lit.; dazu wichtig Rix, MSS 27, 1970, 97]. ,Schwören aus ,fest anfassen [eines Gegenstandes, zur Eidesleistung] war schon idg. entwickelt [210]); dazu auch vyāmá- samāmá-, o. III 438. - Eine iran. Entsprechung zu ant. ,anpacken' in khotansak. näsam- ,to be stilled, cease' < *niž-am- (Bailey bei Emmerick 57)?</p>

अमीवा
<p>अमीवा /amīvā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ámīvā: von ami. ,hart anpacken (s.o. Nachtr. zu ámiti)<br>nicht zu trennen; ámio ist also idg. *azemaz- (gr. ouo-) und kann daher nicht mit gr. àvin (angeblich *ầui-) zusammengehören: Kuiper, AION 1 (1959) 158ff., s. auch Frisk III 33. - Unsicher sind aw. Entsprechungen wie amayavā- ,Leid' (= amivä-/ nach Kuiper a.a.O. 159, der für das Ai. die Analysen ámi-va- oder aber ám-īvā- [d.i. *ageme:- vor Suff. -iya-] zur Wahl stellt) und *anāmīvā, das Bartholomae, BB 8 (1884) 226 für Yasna 49, 10 avāmīrā hergestellt hatte (dazu Humbach II 82) und auf dessen Kontextähnlichkeit mit ved. an-amivá- Schlerath II 158b verweist.</p>

अमू-
<p>अमू- /amū-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>amú-: über *avú- aus *avá stammend (s.u. Nachtr. zu ava-)<br>nach Hauri, KZ 78 (1963) 115ff.</p>

अम्नः
<p>अम्नः /amnaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>amnáh: s. Sharma, Pñua 5/6 (1959/60) 293.</p>

अम्बु
<p>अम्बु /ambu/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ámbu: s. Berger, WZKSOA 3 (1959) 57 Anm. 93 (austroas.;<br>vgl. jedoch die dravid. Sippe von tamil am, âm ,Wasser usw. [DED 15a, DED-Suppl. 33 af.], von der Bloch, BSOAS 5, 739 [,,possibly ... Aryan"; unrichtig referiert o. I 45] und Berger a.a. O. nur die Kurukh-Vertretung kannten (die nach Berger aus der selben Quelle wie ámbu stammt]). — Vorarisches“ ámbu nimmt auch Rix, MSS 27 (1970) 108 Anm. 76 (mit Szemerényi, Syncope 249) an.</p>

अम्भः
<p>अम्भः /ambhaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ámbhaḥl: s. Rix, MSS 27 (1970) 108 Anm. 76. - Vgl. noch<br>W. P. Schmid, Gs. Henning 379.</p>

अम्भः
<p>अम्भः /ambhaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ámbhaḥ: vgl. Wüst, Põua 4 (1958) 100 Anm. 47.</p>

अम्भृणः
<p>अम्भृणः /ambhṛṇaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ambhrnáḥ: $. Rix, MSS 27 (1970) 106 Anm. 45. --- Pāli<br>ammana- usw. (o. I 550f.) hält Turner (briefl. und IAL 30b) wegen singhales. amana, amuna ,a corn-measure' von ambho getrennt. S. auch Burrow, ArchLing. 7 (1955) 151f.</p>

अम्भृणः
<p>अम्भृणः /ambhṛṇaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-630-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ambhrnán, s. Wüst, Pñua 4 (1958) 100 Anm. 47.</p>

अम्लः
<p>अम्लः /amlaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>amláḥ: von Wüst, Pñua 4 (1958) 101 Anm. 54 mit lat. amplus<br>,weit, geräumig verbunden (semantisch wird nhd. stark im Geschmacks- und Geruchsbereich verglichen).</p>

अयः
<p>अयः /ayaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áyah n.: Bed. ,Bronze im älteren Ved. und Aw. nach Eilers,<br>Persica 4 (1969) 23ff. - [Vgl. Rau, Metalle 18 ff.]</p>

अयास्यः
<p>अयास्यः /ayāsyaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ayásyah: nach dem Ansatz von Pischel, Ved. Stud. I 226f.<br>(,,unbändig, wild") ist a-yás-iya- (aw. aiiehijā, „ayehyā.") als nicht zu gürten', ved. a-yás- als ,ohne Gurt' auffaßbar und zu aw. yah- gürten (s. auch 0. III 57) zu stellen (K. Hoffmann briefl.). Eine aw. Entsprechung zu ved. ayássucht R. Schmitt, Or. N.S. 31 (1962) 317ff. im N.pr. Ayo.asti-. -- [Anders wieder Kuiper, IIJ 15 (1973) 180ff. = Charu Deva Shastri Felicitation Volume (1974) 94ff. : a-yás- = not to be injured', zu yā- injure', s.u. Nachtr, zu yātá].</p>

अयोगू-, अयोगूम्
<p>अयोगू-, अयोगूम् /ayogū-/ /ayogūm/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ayogú- f. (VS 30,5 -úm) ,geschwisterloses Mädchen',<br>jünger GșS. u.a. ayugū-; wohl Umformung eines *ayogā-/*ayug- unverbunden (: a-1, yunákti) ,ohne Geschwister nach vadhú- u. dgl. (o. III 136f.). Dazu aw. *ayaoyaēnī- oder *ayŭyaēnī- (in mp. ’ywk'yn' u.a. ,Erbtochter, Erbschwester'), Erweiterung eines entsprechenden aw. *ay(a)ugo: Klingenschmitt, MSS 29 (1971) 168 Anm. 10, mit Lit.</p>

अरघट्टः
<p>अरघट्टः /araghaṭṭaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>araghattaḥ (o. I 551), recte hindi rahat; zu Weiterem s.<br>Turner, IAL 26 bf.</p>

अरटुः
<p>अरटुः /araṭuḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>araṭuḥ: belegt sind AV áratu ~ araduo (s. Whitney, Index<br>Verborum to the Published Text of the Atharva-Veda 33b, Zimmer, Altindisches Leben 62; o. I 551), Kaus., Susr. aralum. ,Calosanthes indica' (Suśr. auch araluka-). Nicht gesichert ist, daß in RV 8, 46, 27 aratvé ein von araṭu- abgeleitetes Adjektiv vorliegt (nach Geldner II 366 vielmehr N. pr.). Vgl. noch prākr. aradu-, lu- m., u.a. (Turner, IAL 27a).</p>

अरडुः
<p>अरडुः /araḍuḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áraduh, s. das Vorige.</p>

अरणः
<p>अरणः /araṇaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áraṇaḥ: dazu nach Mezger, KZ 76 (1960) 178ff. german.<br>*ar-ma- arm', heth. arahza ,ringsum, außerhalb'; dagegen Mayrhofer, Sprache 7 (1961) 180, mit weiterer Lit., Strunk, Fs. Eggers 29 (s. u. 633 zu ármāh]. — Zu beachten Wüst, Põua 12 (1969) 28.</p>

अरत्निः
<p>अरत्निः /aratniḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aratnih: s. auch ratnih, o. III 38.</p>

अरम्
<p>अरम् /aram/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áram: s. Knobloch, Kratylos 4 (1959) 33.</p>

अरमतिः
<p>अरमतिः /aramatiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-632-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-631-632-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>arámatiḥ: vgl. die Lit. bei Wack. II/12 Nachtr. ad 262, 30,<br>pg. 75; Thieme, JAOS 80 (1960) 303b Anm. 10 = Kl. Schr. 398b Anm. 10 (zur Graphie von aw. armasti- [s. zu dessen Übereinstimmungen mit aramati- in Textfiguren Schlerath II 153b, 156b, 158 b]); Atkins, JAOS 81 (1961) 82bff. (vgl. o. III 44 zu ramati-ramáti-); Benveniste, Hitt. 108f.; Bailey, Zor. Probl. xxxiiif.</p>

अरलुः
<p>अरलुः /araluḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>araluh, s. o. die Nachtr. zu aratuh, III 631.</p>

अरविन्दम्
<p>अरविन्दम् /aravindam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aravindam: 8. L. Lombardo, RIL 91 (1957) 235f.; van Win<br>dekens, ZDMG 107 (1957) 554f. (kleinasiat.); für dravid. Ursprung wieder DED 372 a.</p>

अरातिः
<p>अरातिः /arātiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>árátiḥ, 8. o. III 53 (s. v. rātiņi). Vgl. U. Schneider, Der Soma<br>raub des Manu (1971) 48ff.</p>

अरायः
<p>अरायः /arāyaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>árāyaḥ in RV 8, 61, 11 °āsaḥ: nicht einmütig erklärt.<br>Meist als Karge, Geizhälse interpretiert, zu ray-s-ra- (o. III 45f., 52f., bes. III 46), s. Wack. III 215. Dazu RV, AV arāyī f. Unholdin (s. Wack. II/2, 415)? - Bailey, Fs. Gonda 41 Anm. 1 faßt áo als , wild' auf, zu aw. ara., sogd. "r'k ,wild'.</p>

अरिः
<p>अरिः /ariḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>arih: Verteidigung von Thiemes Position in ZDMG 107 (1957)<br>96ff.; dagegen Dumézil, JA 246 (1958) 67 ff., s. auch L'idéologie tripartie des Indo-Européens (1958) 108 ff., de Vries, La Nouvelle Clio 6 (1955) 461 ff., 467, Altnord. etym. Wb. 290b; s. weiteres unter den Nachträgen zu áryaḥ, u. III 633f. - Zu ari-/gr. 104-, ÈQL-s. Schmitt 33f., 131 ff., mit reicher Lit.*); Weiterungen zu ari-/lat. alius (s. bereits Neisser, BB 19 (1893] 133f.) bei Wagner, KZ 75 (1958) 60f. Anm. 4. Weitere Lit. bei Renou, EVédP. 4 (1958) 36. — Eine Stützung von Thiemes Auffassung bietet Abaev, VJa 1958/2, 113ff. (osset. æcæg-ælon foreign' < *hapyaka-aryana- true-stranger'). Bailey, TPS 1959, 106 u. Anm. 4, BSOAS 23 (1960) 19ff. (bes. 19 Anm. 3) postuliert zwei etymologisch verschiedene ari.. Nach Laroche, Hommage à G. Dumézil (1960) 124 ff., 127, 128 ist heth. araya- ,frei', nach Pisani, Paideia 15 (1960) 172 langobard, Ari-manni anzuschließen. Vgl. noch Palmer, Gs. Güntert 11 ff., Ivanov, Etimologija 1971 (1973) 302 ff.<br>*) (Dazu neuestens A. Moreschini Quattordio, Studi e Saggi Linguistici 13 (1973) 185ff.).</p>

अरुणः
<p>अरुणः /aruṇaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>arunáḥ: s. Minard, BSL 51 (1955) c.-r. 38; wichtig Wüst,<br>Pñua 12 (1969) 28f., 47.</p>

अरुषः
<p>अरुषः /aruṣaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aruṣáḥ, 8. u, zu árvā und ásvah, III 634, 636.</p>

अरे
<p>अरे /are/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>are (o. I 50, III 71), vgl. Vogel, Turner-Vol. II (1959) 52 ff.</p>

अर्कः, अर्चति
<p>अर्कः, अर्चति /arkaḥ/ /arcati/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-633-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-632-633-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>arkáh, árcati: vgl. khotansak, aljs- „singen“, Emmerick 11,<br>mit Lit. — Über die Art des Zusammenhanges mit arm. erg 8. Schmitt 259f., mit Lit. (dazu Bailey, Asia Major N.S. 7 [1959] 19 (vielleicht „early loan-word from Iranian", wohl aber Erbwort]; Emmerick a.a.O.). — Zu den semantischen Problemen dieser Sippe („arc-1 : *arc-2") 8. Minard, BSL 51 (1955) c.-r. 38, Burrow, ArchLing. 7 (1955) 153, Emeneau, Lg. 33 (1957) 596, mitLit., Schmid, Kratylos 4 (1959) 49, mit Lit. Vgl. auch Renou, BSL 61 (1966) 7 u. A. 1.- S. noch suvyktih, o. III 489. [Vgl. Joki 254].</p>

अर्जति
<p>अर्जति /arjati/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>árjati: nach Bailey, TPS 1959, 93f., Gs. Sommerfelt 18 u.<br>Anm. 3 zu mp. aržānēnitan ,to obtain', aw. Arajat.aspa. m. N. pr.[?], u.a. – Ai, arjo gehört jedenfalls mit junger Vollstufe I (s. Rix, MSS 27 [1970] 107 Anm. 59) zu r(ñ)jo iraj(o. I 121, 91), in einem semantischen Verhältnis erreichen' ~ ,ausstrecken, recken, richten' (s. schon Whitney, Roots 8. v. ri).</p>

अर्जिः
<p>अर्जिः /arjiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>arjih, s. u. Nachtr. zu rjráḥı.</p>

अर्णः, अर्णस्-
<p>अर्णः, अर्णस्- /arṇaḥ/ /arṇas-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>árnah, árnas- n.: ein árnas-2 ,Reichtum nimmt Bailey, TPS<br>1959, 89 an; dagegen Renou, ÉVédP. 9 (1961) 108, Minard, BSL 58 (1963) c.-r. 57. Nach Bailey a.a.O. 89f. und Burrow, Annals Or. Res. Madras, Centenary Nr. (1957) 4ff. soll auch RV árņa-sāti. als winning of wealth' hierhergehören. - S. noch Manessy-Guitton, IIJ 8 (1964/65) 190 ff., IF 71 (1966) 26f.</p>

अर्त्-
<p>अर्त्- /art-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>art., s. u. rtiyáte Nachtr.</p>

अर्थम्
<p>अर्थम् /artham/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ártham: s. Schlerath II 154 a zu ved. yajñásya ... ártham:<br>aw. arabā ... yasnam, u.a.</p>

अर्दति
<p>अर्दति /ardati/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>árdati: 8. Burrow, Belvalkar-Vol. 3ff. ArchLing. 9 (1957) 133.</p>

अर्भः
<p>अर्भः /arbhaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>árbhaḥ (klein, jung'; iranisch viell, in Namen, s. OnP 154):<br>nach Benveniste, Hitt. 11 f. von den Wörtern für ,Waise' zu trennen (die zu heth. harp- absondern, trennen' gehören sollen); vgl. noch Frisk II 431, III 164, mit weiterer Lit. — (S. auch Joki 297f.].</p>

अर्माः, अर्मक
<p>अर्माः, अर्मक /armāḥ/ /armaka/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ármāḥ, armaká- m. ,Ruinenstätte, Geröll (zur Bed. und den<br>Belegen s. bes. Burrow, Journal of Indian History 41 (1963) 159 ff.), zu verbinden mit got. arms usw. arm®: Strunk, Fs. Eggers 38ff., mit weiterer Lit.</p>

अर्यमा
<p>अर्यमा /aryamā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aryamá, vgl. Schlerath II 160a; s. ferner die Nachtr. zu áryaḥ.</p>

अर्यः, आर्यः
<p>अर्यः, आर्यः /aryaḥ/ /āryaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-634-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-633-634-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áryaḥ (: áryah), s. die Nachträge zu arih, o. III 632; vgl.<br>noch bes. Thieme, Mitra and Aryaman (Transactions of the Connecticut Academy of Arts and Sciences Vol. 41, 1957) 72ff.; Bailey, University of Ceylon Review 15 (1957) 33, TPS 1959, 71ff. [bes. zu *arya- ,wealth', S. 78 zur Analyse von arya-mán-, 84f. zu árya- ,owner of wealth', 85 zu ariowner', 99f. zu idg. *ario-, 101ff. zu ai. árya-, usw.), TPS 1960, 87f.; Palmer, Gs. Güntert 11 ff. (Vgl. Joki 297].</p>

अर्वा
<p>अर्वा /arvā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>árvā mit ugráh, vgl. aw.atrvato ... ugrăng; árvantam ... arusám,<br>vgl. aw. a'ruša a'rvanta, u.a.: Schmitt bei Schlerath II 159 a, 160 a.</p>

अर्वान्
<p>अर्वान् /arvān/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>arván: s. noch Bailey, BSOAS 21 (1958) 535f.</p>

अर्शः
<p>अर्शः /arśaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ársah: dazu sogd. Ärsy, 'ro'ny ,Hämorrhoiden', H[enning] bei<br>Gershevitch 62 (8 4031).</p>

अलकम्
<p>अलकम् /alakam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>álakam (sub Alakā, o. I 53): zur Etymologie (als ,vergeblich<br>zu kl. alam = ved. áram) s. schon Renou, JA 231 (1939) 174 Anm. 1 (etwas anders Wack. III 447); eine neue Deutung bei Bailey, BSOAS 24 (1961) 477 (áo - in a wild ... way'). Zu Wüsts Auffassung vgl. Põua 7 (1961) 133 Anm. 12, mit weiterer Lit.; s. noch Renou, ÉVédP. 16 (1967) 141, 161.</p>

अलजिः
<p>अलजिः /alajiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>alajih (tumour' nach Tarapada Chowdhury, JBORS 17, 38f.,<br>lt. Kuiper, Museum 64 (1959) 211): vielleicht dravidisch (: tamil aral ,to burn', ararci ,burning sensation' usw.), s. DED 21a (Nr. 234).</p>

अलर्कः
<p>अलर्कः /alarkaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>alarkaḥ (,,toller Hund“, o. I 54, Kleindruck): Nach Burrow,<br>De Vol. 45f. zu aw. ara- ,wild', lit. aliótis ,Rasereien begehen', usw.; zur selben Reduplikationsform *al-al- (> al-aro) soll auch alarti (RV "goes astray”, nicht zu rnótil) gehören, Burrow a.a. O.</p>

अलर्ति
<p>अलर्ति /alarti/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>alarti, s. das Vorangehende.</p>

अलला, अललाभवन्त्-
<p>अलला, अललाभवन्त्- /alalā/ /alalābhavant-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>alală (obhávant-): gegen Thieme (o. I 552) s. Edgerton, JAOS<br>79 (1959) 43b.</p>

अलातम्
<p>अलातम् /alātam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>alātam, vgl. Bailey, TPS 1955, 81f. -- Wegen der Nebenform<br>*lāta- (hindi lai usw., Turner, IAL 31b) hält Kuiper, IIJ 7 (1963/64) 319 austroasiatischen Ursprung für möglich.</p>

अलातृणः
<p>अलातृणः /alātṛṇaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>alātrnáh (o. I 552): s. Renou, ÉVédP. 10 (1962) 71.</p>

अलिक्लवः
<p>अलिक्लवः /aliklavaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aliklavah: auch Jaim.-Br. II 440; AVPaipp. XVI 104, 2<br>ariklava-; Kātha-Brāhm. arikravi. (nach L. v. Schroeder, SbAkWien 137 (1897] IV 14 zu kravés-). [Hinweise von K. Hoffmann.]</p>

अलिञ्जरः
<p>अलिञ्जरः /aliñjaraḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-12.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-12.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aliñjaraḥ: eine austroasiat. Deutung bei Berger, WZKSOA 3<br>(1959) 58; doch s. Kuiper, IIJ 7 (1963/64) 319, 323. — Vgl. Agrawala, Mél. Renou 9 Anm. 1.</p>

अलीकः
<p>अलीकः /alīkaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-635-13.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-634-635-13.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>alikaḥ (Akzentangabe [s. o. I 552] ist zu streichen, s. Wüst,<br>Pñua 8-11 [1966] 18f., mit Lit.), vgl. Bailey, BSOAS 24 (1961) 477, 26 (1963) 89, Wüst a.a. O. Gershovitch, Fs. Pagliaro II (1969) 205.</p>

अल्कः
<p>अल्कः /alkaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>alkaḥ, s. u. die Nachtr. zu vyálkaśā.</p>

अल्गौ
<p>अल्गौ /algau/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>algáu: s. L. Lombardo, RIL 91 (1957) 236f.</p>

अव
<p>अव /ava/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áva: vgl. die Nebenform vao, dazu Wack. II/1, 72, I2 Nachtr.<br>ad 79, 14, pg. 45, weitere Beispiele bei Pisani, Väk 2 (1952) 20; wohl nicht hierher vadánya-, s.o. III 134.</p>

अव-
<p>अव- /ava-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ava-: ved. avóh wird als Gen.-Lok. Du. zu avá- abgelehnt von<br>Hauri, KZ 78 (1963) 116 ff., der andererseits *avá (= aksl. ov) als Vorform von amú - (s. o. Nachtr., III 630) annimmt. Dazu Strunk, KZ 83 (1969) 54 A. 8.</p>

अवति
<p>अवति /avati/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>avati, s.u. Nachtr. zu uvé.</p>

अवनिः
<p>अवनिः /avaniḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>avániņi (dazu avánih, da von Flußbett auszugehen ist:<br>Wüst, Põua 8-11 [1966] 271 Anm. 18, mit weiterer Lit.): 8. Wüst a.a.O. 269; vgl. noch Bailey, Zamb. 317.</p>

अवप्रज्जनम्
<p>अवप्रज्जनम् /avaprajjanam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>avaprajjanam, s. o. II 330, u. prņákti.</p>

अवरः
<p>अवरः /avaraḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ávaraḥ, s. noch várākah, o. III 150.</p>

अवः
<p>अवः /avaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ávaḥ: vgl. Textfiguren wie ávasā ... [sám] gamo ~ aw.jamyāt<br>avarhe u.a., ávase havo ~ zbayat avanhe (o. III 586), Schlerath II 158b, 163 a. — Von avas-yo (o. I 552) ist ap. patiyāvahyaiy wohl fernzuhalten, s. die Lit. in OnP 109.</p>

अविमरीसम्
<p>अविमरीसम् /avimarīsam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>avimarisam n. Schafsmilch (Gramm.): marisa- ist nach<br>Burrow, BSOAS 33 (1970) 46 LW aus iran. *mar(i)za-= nhd. Milch usw.; s. noch u. die Nachträge zu dūsa-, sodha-.</p>

अविः
<p>अविः /aviḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áviņ: dazu luw. ha-a-ú-i-viš, hier.-heth. ha-WA-a-8 (haw[i]a-),<br>lyk. xava- moutono; Benveniste, Hitt. 12f., Laroche, Dictionnaire de la langue louvite (1959) 44f., 151, BSL 62 (1968) 59f., mit Lit.</p>

अश्नाति
<p>अश्नाति /aśnāti/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-12.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-12.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aśnáti: Anders über aw. kahrkāsa- Bailey, TPS 1954, 145f.<br>— Zu ai. as- wird noch aw. asito in Yasna 10, 14 gestellt, s. Bartholomae 338 (und Zum Airan. Wb. 222, mit Lit.), bzw. Lommel, ZII 1 (1922) 32 u. Anm. 1.</p>

अश्नोति
<p>अश्नोति /aśnoti/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-13.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-13.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aśnóti: Vgl. ved. ksatrám āśāte ~ aw. hšaþrā nasat, Schlerath<br>II 159b. – Recte aw. ašnaoo; vgl. noch Klingenschmitt, MSS 28 (1970) 71.</p>

अश्मा
<p>अश्मा /aśmā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-14.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-14.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áśmā: Zur Zugehörigkeit von got. himins s. Schindler, Kratylos<br>15 (1970[72]) 152. - (Vgl. Maher, JIES 1 (1973) 441 ff.].</p>

अश्रिः
<p>अश्रिः /aśriḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-15.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-635-15.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áśrih: s. Wüst, Pñua 4 (1958) 31 f.</p>

अश्वत्थः
<p>अश्वत्थः /aśvatthaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>asvattháh: Die Problematik dieses Wortes und anderer Wörter<br>auf ottha- bleibt weiterhin offen, s. o. I 238 (und I 565), II 612, III 528 (mit Lit.). Neuere Äußerungen neigen sich wieder der Deutung als *asva-atha- ,Pferde-Standort zu (Ficus religiosa in der ved. Literatur das irdische Abbild des mythischen Weltbaumes; bei den Mongolen ist der Weltbaum ein Pfahl, an den die zirkumpolaren Sterne [,,Pferde"] angebunden sind und um den sie kreisen, Lommel briefl., s. auch Paideuma 6 [1958] 493 (vgl. U. Holmberg, Der Baum des Lebens, Helsinki 1922]; de Vries, Altgermanische Religionsgeschichte II [1957] 391). S. noch Wayman, IIJ 3 (1959) 125; OnP 129. - [Nach K. Hoffmann (briefl.) ist asvatthá- *asva-d-tha. ,Pferdefral' (ähnlich s. zu kapio, kula. Nachtr.); vgl. gr. XOLOTOV < *aiepi-OTO- (*od-to-) eig. ,in der Frühe gegessen'. -- S. ferner Ivanov, PIJKNI 75ff.]<br>den sie kry. Holmberg; manische</p>

अश्ववारः
<p>अश्ववारः /aśvavāraḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>asvavärah: Weiteres zum Iran. bei Morgenstierne 71 und<br>ApH 106.</p>

अश्वसनिः
<p>अश्वसनिः /aśvasaniḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>asvasánih (so zu akzentuieren]: mit dem Kikkuli-Titel<br>aššuššanni nicht gleichsetzbar; s. die Lit. bei MIAV 130a, 136 a, dazu Kammenhuber, Arier 209.</p>

अश्वः
<p>अश्वः /aśvaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ásvah: Vgl. ved. áśvā ... arusásah ~ aw. aspahe ... a'rušahe;<br>ved. dopam [...] nay v aw.aspa... mao, ap. a8am frãnagam; ved. āśvdsva- usw. (o. I 83) ~ hom. oxées intov; ved. áśvāsaḥ ... rārahānáhr aw. ranjat.aspam, usw., S. Schlerath II 161 a, 161, 162 af., 164b, Schmitt 238ff. - Gegen áśvā f. ,Stuteals Erbwort' s. richtig Cardona, Lg. 36 (1960) 535 u. Anm. 5, mit Lit. — Zur reichen Diskussion über mögliche Entlehnungen aus indoar. *ašva(O)- bzw. zu seiner Repräsen. tanz in der Sprache der vorderasiatischen Arier s. die Verweise bei MIAV 130a, Kammenhuber, Arier 253b, Mayrhofer, Mythos 15 Anm. 21, 19, 33 Anm. 106.</p>

अष्टा
<p>अष्टा /aṣṭā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>astá, s. die Lit. bei Szemerényi, Syncope 399f.</p>

अष्टिः
<p>अष्टिः /aṣṭiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aṣṭih Samenkorn' (Lex. asthi., 8. noch Turner, IAL 42b), vgl.<br>Hiersche, Aspirata 58f., 135; ebenda auch zu asthila (o. I 63f.).</p>

अष्ट्रा
<p>अष्ट्रा /aṣṭrā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ástră, s. Hiersche, Aspirata 57f.</p>

असक्रः
<p>असक्रः /asakraḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ásakrah, vgl. noch o. III 227 (visaktā) und HII 418 (zu sac->,<br>sa-óc- usw. „stocken“).</p>

असितः
<p>असितः /asitaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ásitaḥ: iran. *ahita- dunkel' vielleicht in khotansak. hätänaa<br>,rot', Bailey, Zamb. 413f.-S. auch unten den Nachtr.zu asih.</p>

असिदः
<p>असिदः /asidaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-637-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-636-637-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>asidah: Nach K. Hoffmann (briefi.) zu asih Messer und da.<br>„schneiden, mähen', also „mit dem Messer mähend“ (im Unterschied zu Pferde- und Ochsenrippe, die ebenfalls zum Grasschneiden verwendet wurden, s. Ap.S.S. I 3, 1).</p>

असिन्वः
<p>असिन्वः /asinvaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>asinváh: 8. o. III 466 (zu sinam); vgl. auch Bailey, BSOAS 21<br>(1958) 531 (und o. III 465), Renou, ÉVédP. 4 (1958) 102.</p>

असिः
<p>असिः /asiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>asih: Nach Thieme, Lg. 34 (1958) 512ff. ursprünglich „das<br>schwarze (Metallj", so wie lat. ēnsis (also keine „idg." Gleichung für Eisen"); mit gr. aois zur Farbbezeichnung ásitaḥ (o. I 64, 553, III 636) gehörig (wie hári- : hárita-, róhi. : róhita-). – Dazu Leumann, Glo. 42 (1964) 108.</p>

असुरः
<p>असुरः /asuraḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ásurah und ásuh: Vgl. Schlerath, Fs. Kuiper 142 ff. (mit Lit.,<br>bes. 146; dazu Pisani, Handes Amsorya 75 [1961] 552 u. Anm. 5), nach dem ar. *asu-ra- ,Herr' zu heth. hašš- ,zeugen', aw. ahu- ,Herr = heth. haššu- ,König, lat. erus gehört, während ásu. „Leben, Existenz' (nicht , Lebensatem, Orenda) bedeute und zu aw. ahu-, ahva- ,Leben' (: as ,sein“) zu stellen sei. Vgl. auch Burrow, JRAS 1973, 127f. Zu indo-iran. Textfiguren mit ásu-sahu-: Schlerath a.a. 0. 152f. und Schlerath II 151a, 155b, 164a, 164b (3mal); zu solchen mit ásura- ahura- Schlerath II 150b, 151 a. — [8. noch Joki 253).</p>

असूर्त-
<p>असूर्त- /asūrta-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>asúrta-, s. zu súrta- o. III 495f. und u. Bd. III Nachtr.</p>

असृक्
<p>असृक् /asṛk/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ás;k: Iran. *ahro (= ásy-k) in mp. *āro vermutet Gershevitch,<br>IF 75 (1970[71]) 306.</p>

असौ
<p>असौ /asau/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>asáu: Vgl. Benveniste, Hitt. 71f.; Klingenschmitt, MSS 30 :<br>(1972) 99.</p>

अस्तम्
<p>अस्तम् /astam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ástam: zu as- ,sein' nach Collinder, Språkvetensk. Sällskapets<br>i Uppsala Förhandlingar 1954:10 (1952-54) 84, 85.</p>

अस्ता
<p>अस्ता /astā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ástā, s. ved. ástāra iṣum, isumān ... ástā ~ aw. asta išum,<br>Schlerath II 164 b.</p>

अस्ति
<p>अस्ति /asti/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ásti: Zu indo-iran. Textfiguren mit as-lah- s.o. I 553, Schle<br>rath II 150b, 151 bf., 153b, 156 a, 158a, 158 b, 160a. – Über die Annahme eines *218-29 - (ai. să-) ,sein' s. o. III 455 (sátuh), 459 (s. v. sáma); zur Problematik von stí- (osti-) ~ as-(?) 8. o. III 514. --- Hierher als substantivierte Verbform RV usw. svasti- f. ,Wohlsein, Heil, Segen' (erst jünger astiastio, s. Liebert 47f.; Yājñ. u.a. ästi-ka- gläubig'), davon svastika- m.,eine Glück bringende Figur, Svastika' (ep., kl.); Liebert a.a. O., Wack. II/2,638. S. auch o. Nachtr. zu ástam und s.v. ásurah über ásu- ,Existenz'.</p>

अस्थि
<p>अस्थि /asthi/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-638-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-637-638-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ásthi: Vgl. Kellens, Diss. 598ff. - Erhaltenes slav, *osto (<br>ásthi; sonst slav. *kostb, s. dazu Schmitt-Brandt 107) nach Machek, ZSIPhil. 28 (1960) 161 noch in aksl. ostong usw. ,Stachel' (?).</p>

अस्रम्
<p>अस्रम् /asram/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>asram: Über asra- n. ,Träne' (: áśru) und heth. ešhahru<br>išhahru- , Tränenstrom, Weinen's. Ivanov, Studia Linguistica in honorem S. Mladenov (Sofia 1957) 477ff. – [Nach K. Hoffmann (briefl.) gehört das Singulare tantum asram nicht zu áśru, sondern ist identisch mit Jaim.-Br, asram ,Leid, Schmerz = aw. anra- schlecht, böse'; vgl. auch TB II 7, 13, 2 asró ádrih ,der schmerzhafte (der geworfene?) Stein'.]</p>

अस्रः
<p>अस्रः /asraḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>asráḥ, s. o. Nachtr. zu asram.</p>

अहन्यः, अहना-
<p>अहन्यः, अहना- /ahanyaḥ/ /ahanā-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ahanyàḥ, ahand-, s. u. Nachtr. zu āhandh, ITI 642.</p>

अहर्-
<p>अहर्- /ahar-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áhar-: s. Schulze, Kl. Schr.2 (1966; Nachträge ed. W. Wiss<br>mann) 824f., 845f. - Hierher Br. āhnáya ,für immer, woraus (mit Kürzung vor Doppelkonsonanz) ep., kl. ahnāya ,sofort, sogleich', vgl. noch im Mahābh. ahnaya ca cirāya ca ,für immer und ewig'; K. Hoffmann, IIJ 4 (1960) 14f.</p>

अहल्लिक-
<p>अहल्लिक- /ahallika-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ahallika- år. ney. (ŚB 14, 6, 9, 26 = BỊhadĀrUp. 3, 9,<br>25): „Nobody knows what it means (except that it is a Schimpfwort'), and I don't think the guesses in BR and the translations have any value ..." (F. Edgerton, briefl. 6. 10. 1960). Vermutungen bei Minard, Énigmes I 81 (223 a), Sharma, Pñua 5/6 (1959/60) 57.</p>

अहिः
<p>अहिः /ahiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áhiḥ: Fortsetzer von german. *agiz Schlange, Drache' bei<br>Plassmann, Sonderband zu PBB (Halle) 82 (Festschr. E. Karg-Gasterstädt, 1961) 94ff.</p>

अह्नाय
<p>अह्नाय /ahnāya/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ahnāya, s.o. Nachtr. zu áhar..</p>

अह्रि-
<p>अह्रि- /ahri-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áhri- (nur RV 9, 54, 1 ayaḥ), RV áhraya-, áhrayāņa-:<br>gewöhnlich (als etwa ,keck, üppig, nicht schüchtern) wie SB á-hri- schamlos' zu hri- gestellt (o. I 436, Wack. II/2, 273, III 187 [s. d.]); anders Wüst, Põua 4 (1958) 30f.</p>

आ
<p>आ /ā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-639-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-638-639-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>đi (khotangak. &-, SOgd.”., parth.”., Emmerick 229): zur<br>Etymologie und zum Zusammenhang mit ahd. uo-, ae. Öusw. s. Steinhauser, Zeitschr. f. Mundartforschg. 27 (1960) 102 ff.</p>

आकाशः
<p>आकाशः /ākāśaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>akāsáh: Gegen Garbes Entlehnungstheorie zu Recht Wüst,<br>Pñua 12 (1967/68) 107, mit Lit.</p>

आकुलः
<p>आकुलः /ākulaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>akulaḥ, s. sankulah, o. III 416 (*-krpo-?).</p>

आखरः
<p>आखरः /ākharaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ākharáḥ: s. Hiersche, Aspirata 89, mit der älteren Lit.</p>

आगः
<p>आगः /āgaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ágan: Zur Trennung von gr. ayos (o. I 553, Frisk III 17,<br>Chantraine I 13b) s. auch Schmitt 24, mit weiterer Lit.</p>

आङ्गूषः
<p>आङ्गूषः /āṅgūṣaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>angūsáh, s. o. III 624 zu angosí.</p>

आच्छोटः, आच्छोदनम्
<p>आच्छोटः, आच्छोदनम् /ācchoṭaḥ/ /ācchodanam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ācchoṭaḥ m., ācchodanam (v. 1. ākṣo) n. Jagd (Lex.):<br>s. Hiersche, Aspirata 113.</p>

आटोपः
<p>आटोपः /āṭopaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ātopaḥ: Wüst, Pñua 3 (1957) 75 ff. ; Burrow, BSOAS 34 (1971)<br>551.</p>

आडम्बरः
<p>आडम्बरः /āḍambaraḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ādambaraḥ: Wüst, Põua 2 (1956) 46 Anm. 22.</p>

आढकः
<p>आढकः /āḍhakaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ādhakaḥ: Fragend mit Dravidischem verknüpft in DED 29 a<br>(Nr. 339); dazu Mayrhofer, Kratylos 6 (1961) 158.</p>

आढ्यः
<p>आढ्यः /āḍhyaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ädhyáh: Zweifel an der Deutung aus arthya- bei Turner, IAL<br>50a; Neuvorschläge bei Wüst, Pñua 4 (1958) 55 Anm. 10, bzw. Liebert, Orientalia Suecana 13 (1964) 136 ff. -- Vgl. Burrow, BSOAS 35 (1972) 542.</p>

आणिः
<p>आणिः /āṇiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>āniņ: s. Kuiper, IIJ 7 (1963/64) 323; Burrow, BSOAS 35 (1972)<br>543.</p>

आतिः
<p>आतिः /ātiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-12.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-12.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ātiņ: Iranisches (v.a. osset. acc/accæ ,Wildente') bei Abajew I<br>27. — Turner, IAL 51a nimmt wieder ats- und die Formen mit -t-/-d- zusammen (anders o. I 554); auf aṭi- geht „all I[ndo]A[ryan] including Kafiri and Dardic" zurück (Turner briefl. und a.a.O.). – Vgl. auch Beekes 197.</p>

आत्मा
<p>आत्मा /ātmā/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-13.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-13.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ātmá: Zu ão, tmán-/tán- (o. I 528f.) 8. Edgerton, Lg. 38 (1962)<br>354. — Etymologisch mit aw. ätarš Feuer', gr. nrog ,Herz' verbunden von Humbach I 32 A. 47, Innsbr. Tagg. 123; ganz anders Thieme, KZ 86 (1972) 81 (*[a-]kt-mán- zu cat- „schleichen' [,Atem' = ,der Schleichende, leise Gehende', im Gegen. satz zum Wind]).</p>

आध्रः
<p>आध्रः /ādhraḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-14.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-14.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>adhráh:s. Wüst, Põua 3 (1957) 118, 4 (1958) 45ff. (mit reicher<br>Lit.).</p>

आनुषक्
<p>आनुषक् /ānuṣak/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-15.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-639-15.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ānusák: s. G. Ito, Acta Asiatica (Tokyo] 26 (1974) 62.</p>

आन्दम्
<p>आन्दम् /āndam/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-01.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-01.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>āndam, s. u. andam Nachtr., o. III 626.</p>

आपः
<p>आपः /āpaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-02.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-02.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ápaḥ1: Vgl. RV ápah ... bhesajih u.a. ~ aw. āpo ... baēšazyå,<br>RV ávāsrjah ... apáḥ ~ aw. āpó hərəzayən (Schmitt bei Schlerath II 163b), RV 7, 34, 3 ápah ... prthuth ~ Yašt 10, 14 apo ... para wiš (Schm.). — Hierher heth. hapā ,Fluß', Friedrich, 2. Ergänz.-Heft zum Heth. Wb. (1961) 11a; s. Watkins, BSL 67 (1972) 39 ff. [sowie Hamp, MSS 30 (1972) 35ff., Laroche, Fs. Otten 187f., Watkins, Ériu 24 (1973) 82 ff. (s.d.!)]. — S. auch Wagner, ZfCPh. 33 (1974) 1 ff.</p>

आपिः
<p>आपिः /āpiḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-03.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-03.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>āpih, s. Minard, BSL 56 (1961) c.-r. 60, mit Lit.</p>

आपीडः
<p>आपीडः /āpīḍaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-04.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-04.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>āpidaḥ: 8. Berger, Fs. Scherer 67.</p>

आप्त्यः
<p>आप्त्यः /āptyaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-05.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-05.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>aptyáh: S. Wright, BSOAS 30 (1967) 544; Gershevitch, Fs.<br>Pagliaro II 188f. (dazu OnP 131).</p>

आप्नोति
<p>आप्नोति /āpnoti/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-06.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-06.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>äpnóti: RV ksatrám . . . āpúh ~ aw. apāno ... hšapram u.a.,<br>Schlerath II 154 a.</p>

आप्री
<p>आप्री /āprī/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-07.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-07.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>āprí: S. o. II 380 und Schlerath II 164 (ad A 1,8).</p>

आमयति
<p>आमयति /āmayati/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-08.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-08.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>āmáyati, s. o. III 630 Nachtr. zu ámiti.</p>

आमयः, -आमय-
<p>आमयः, -आमय- /āmayaḥ/ /-āmaya-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-09.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-09.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>āmayan, "āmaya- (o I 554): ursprünglich ,Beschädigung , vgl.<br>MS amayāvin- ,injuring' u.a.; von ámīvā zu trennen (s.o. III 630) und zu a-mi- ,hinschwinden lassen' gehörig ( mináti, o. II 636).</p>

आमरीतर्-, अमुर्-, अमुरि-
<p>आमरीतर्-, अमुर्-, अमुरि- /āmarītar-/ /amur-/ /amuri-/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-10.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-10.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ämarītár-, amúr(i)., s. u. mrņáti? Nachtr.</p>

आमः
<p>आमः /āmaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-11.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-11.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ämáh: Weiteres Iranische (zu o. I 554) wie khotansak. häma<br>roh', sogd. y'm'kw bei Bailey, Zamb. 408.</p>

आमिः, आमिष
<p>आमिः, आमिष /āmiḥ/ /āmiṣa/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-12.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-12.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>ámih, āmiṣd-: für Kuipers Deutung (s.o. I 77) tritt Burrow,<br>De Vol. 46 ff. ein (s. auch u. Nachtr. zu mistah). - Awest. āmiš wird von Duchesne-Guillemin, JA 228 (1936) 247 wiederhergestellt.</p>

आमुपः
<p>आमुपः /āmupaḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-13.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-13.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>āmupah m. Bambusa spinosa (Lex.); viell. dravidisch,<br>vgl. tamil āmpal ,bamboo', āmal „spiny bambooʻ, DED-Suppl. 33 a.</p>

आयुः
<p>आयुः /āyuḥ/ <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-14.jpg'>IMG</a> <a href='https://github.com/sanskrit/samskrtam.ru/blob/master/backup/sanskrit-lexicon/KEWA/src/img/3-640-14.jpg.txt'>Edit</a> </p><p><br><br>áyuḥ: Dazu yúvan-, yúḥ (o. III 23f., 24f., mit Lit.); *ayu<br>wohl auch in Kompp. wie dirgháyu- (II 47, Schlerath II 164 af.), s. Schmitt 162 u. Anm. 971c (mit Lit.); vgl. noch Beekes 105, 128, Chantraine I 43 a, Frisk III 21. -- Zum Ansatz eines von áyu(s). zu trennenden ayú- ,teacher' s. Bailey, BSOAS 20 (1957) 41ff., 21 (1958) 536 ff.</p>

